OrionLayer open fix 122 — the reply to a human player's diplomacy request on the wire
====================================================================================

Work order 408. orion2re on the fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.0), on top
of open fix 121 and its README row. Not on `orionlayer-local`. In
src/game/mainscr.cpp under ORION2RE_EXT, and a comment row in
src/ext/ext_api.cpp's TPOP table.

In a network game (game type 2 or 3) the main screen's loop calls
MAINSCR::Check_For_Diplomacy_Request (mainscr_main.cpp:394-396,
mainscr.cpp:2646-2675) every pass: when NETMOX::Human_Requesting_Diplomacy
names a player, MAINSCR::Do_Reply_To_Diplomacy_Request (mainscr.cpp:2475-2540)
runs ITS OWN input loop over the map — the popup of BUFFER0.LBX 0x0F with
three buttons: ACCEPT (0x10, hotkey A, reply 1: Accept_Diplomacy_Request,
which opens the diplomacy screen), IGNORE (0x11, hotkey I, reply 2:
Refuse_Diplomacy_Request) and WAIT (0x12, hotkey W, reply 3:
Tell_Diplomacy_Requester_To_Wait), and the message H_Message 0xDB over the
requester's name and race name (Draw_Reply_To_Diplomacy_Request,
mainscr.cpp:4732-4752). It is NOT started by a click on the request light
(Draw_Diplomacy_Request_Lights, :1067-1100, draws and has no field). ESC is a
hidden whole-screen field whose handle is thrown away (`unused_field`), so it
selects nothing and the loop goes on. Right click: help 677 over the popup,
678 / 679 / 680 on the buttons (evanhelp.cpp:140-145, :516-530). The loop is
a modal one with its own fields; nothing of it reached a client but pixels
and a field list under the caller's id.

The change. While the loop runs a TurnPopupGuard reports id 88 and TPOP
kind 26 (no new block, no new version: TPOP is version 1 for every kind but
the Turn Summary's): args [0] the requester, [1] the accept field, [2] the
invoke field (reply 2, Refuse), [3] the wait field, [4] the requester's
colour (-1 when the requester is out of range); text = the message formatted
once before the loop, as the drawing function formats it (H 0xDB, name, race
name), into a buffer that outlives the loop; title empty; no tail. The guard
ends when the loop does. Read only; nothing in the game's play changes.

Live: UNVERIFIED — see doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md entry 122: a network game
cannot be started offline, and the hotseat game (the project's only live
path) never has a request (NETMOX::human_diplomacy_request_mask is set by
the network layer only). Built as a syntax check of the changed files against
the build's own flags and PCH on the scratch clone
`~/claude/clones/408_orion2re` (ORION2RE_EXT on; a misspelt variable is
refused by the compiler); ~/orion2re/out is not rebuilt by this work.

